Z||000007||LT1 Chop Top||09-02-2001||10:39 PM||||Dragon,<P>The Blue Chop Top preforms like a stock Fiero under 'regular' driving, very light and nimble, as long as you don't romp on it.  What little extra weight the engine adds is not noticable (compared to my stock engine 88GT).  This car is incredibly powerful...over twice as powerful as a V6, simply put...it flys!  I have never had any official #'s but I have never lost a street race (Honda, Mustang, Camaro).  I have learned NOT to accellerate into corners to keep from spinning out, and I can easily spin the tires into 3rd gear.  Check out the MPEG's of the car doing 100MPH passes here: <A HREF="http://ucsub.colorado.edu/~pattons/Home15.html" TARGET=_blank>http://ucsub.colorado.edu/~pattons/Home15.html</A>   It has a stock 87 Getrag 5-speed.  Thanks for the compliments, but V8 Archie gets all the credit.<BR>Beer-stud,<BR>I am 6'2" and I fit fine....the seats have been shallowed about 1" to help compensate for the chop.||||reg||10
